WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.440
Capacity doesn't override the rest of the design.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.620
The protective bonding and return scheme still follows the cited implementation.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.000
Thermal conditions still determine whether the applicable component and assembly ratings are

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:11.440
supported.

5
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.960
Service access still has to accommodate the approved isolation and replacement method.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.320
A high-current connection may be inaccessible after neighboring equipment and hoses are

7
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:20.820
installed.

8
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.580
A cooling change may alter the conditions under which a distribution assembly

9
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.240
was qualified.

10
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.020
A revised shelf can change both management and physical interfaces.

11
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.360
These are integration changes, not paperwork details.

12
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.160
Review the complete populated rack and the allowed maintenance state with the

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.100
qualified teams.

14
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.280
Record the operating limits and any required restrictions.

15
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.800
The course doesn't authorize energized work or establish safe access distances.

16
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.940
Its purpose is to make sure those responsibilities and approved conditions are

17
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.900
represented in the deployment decision, rather than omitted because the power calculation

18
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.840
appeared to pass.

